IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ea3-schedules`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- ea3: TESTS FOR THE FIVE SCHEDULES.
-- Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text of the Schedules (the lines cited beside each group),
-- never copied from what the code printed.  Dates are written `Date day month year`.
-- 4 January 2026 is a Sunday (a calendar), so 5 January 2026 is a Monday.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fixtures
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A pay record with only the items a test needs; every other item is nil.
GIVEN work IS A NUMBER
      overtime IS A NUMBER
      bonus IS A NUMBER
      productivity IS A NUMBER
      reimbursement IS A NUMBER
      travelling IS A NUMBER
      food IS A NUMBER
      housing IS A NUMBER
      `other allowances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pay for a period`
`ea3 test pay` MEANS
    `Pay for a period` WITH
        `the amounts are for` IS `Pay is fixed for each month`
        `pay for the work, with wage adjustments and increments` IS work
        `overtime payments` IS overtime
        `bonus payments or annual wage supplements` IS bonus
        `commissions` IS 0
        `productivity incentive payments` IS productivity
        `sums paid to reimburse special expenses incurred in the course of employment` IS reimbursement
        `travelling allowances` IS travelling
        `food allowances` IS food
        `housing allowances` IS housing
        `allowances of any other kind` IS `other allowances`
        `value of house accommodation, electricity, water, medical attendance or other amenity` IS 0
        `value of a service excluded by order of the Minister` IS 0
        `value of a travelling concession` IS 0
        `employer's contributions on its own account to a pension fund or provident fund` IS 0
        `gratuity payable on discharge or retirement` IS 0
        `retrenchment benefit payable on retrenchment` IS 0

GIVEN full IS A NUMBER
      half IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 3 Days required in a week`
`ea3 test sch 3 week` MEANS
    `sch 3 Days required in a week` WITH
        `days required to work for more than 5 hours` IS full
        `days required to work for 5 hours or less` IS half

-- The weeks the caller gives, routed to the paragraph the purpose names: `preceding` is limb (i) and `alternative` limb (ii)
-- of that paragraph; the other paragraphs' weeks are left empty.
GIVEN purpose IS A `sch 3 item 5 Purpose of the calculation`
      `less than 3 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
      preceding IS A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
      alternative IS A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
GIVETH A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` MEANS
    `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average` WITH
        `the purpose of the calculation` IS purpose
        `the employee was in employment for less than 3 weeks` IS `less than 3 weeks`
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the termination of the contract` IS (IF purpose EQUALS `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` THEN preceding ELSE (LIST))
        `the first 3 weeks of the employee's employment` IS (IF purpose EQUALS `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` THEN alternative ELSE (LIST))
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of absence or period of absence` IS (IF purpose EQUALS `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` THEN preceding ELSE (LIST))
        `the 3 weeks immediately following the day of absence or period of absence` IS (IF purpose EQUALS `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` THEN alternative ELSE (LIST))
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS (IF purpose EQUALS `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` THEN preceding ELSE (LIST))
        `the 3 weeks immediately following the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS (IF purpose EQUALS `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` THEN alternative ELSE (LIST))

-- Six different lists, one per limb, so that the paragraph read can be told from the others.
-- (a)(i) 5, 5, 2 averages 4; (a)(ii) 5, 3, 6 averages 14/3; (b)(i) 1, 1, 1 averages 1; (b)(ii) 2, 2, 2 averages 2;
-- (c)(i) 3, 3, 3 averages 3; (c)(ii) 6, 6, 6 averages 6.
GIVEN purpose IS A `sch 3 item 5 Purpose of the calculation`
      `less than 3 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` MEANS
    `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average` WITH
        `the purpose of the calculation` IS purpose
        `the employee was in employment for less than 3 weeks` IS `less than 3 weeks`
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the termination of the contract` IS `ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`
        `the first 3 weeks of the employee's employment` IS `ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of absence or period of absence` IS `ea3 test sch 3 weeks 1 1 1`
        `the 3 weeks immediately following the day of absence or period of absence` IS `ea3 test sch 3 weeks 2 2 2`
        `the 3 weeks immediately preceding the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS `ea3 test sch 3 weeks 3 3 3`
        `the 3 weeks immediately following the rest day, holiday, day of leave or period of leave` IS `ea3 test sch 3 weeks 6 6 6`

-- The three weeks 5, 5 and 2 days: item 7 gives 5, 5 and 2, whose average is 4.
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2` MEANS
    LIST `ea3 test sch 3 week` 5 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 5 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 2 0

-- The three weeks 4+2 half days, 3 and 6: item 7 gives 5, 3 and 6, whose average is 14/3.
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6` MEANS
    LIST `ea3 test sch 3 week` 4 2
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 3 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 6 0

-- Three weeks of 1 days each: item 7 gives 1, whose average is 1.
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 1 1 1` MEANS
    LIST `ea3 test sch 3 week` 1 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 1 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 1 0

-- Three weeks of 2 days each: item 7 gives 2, whose average is 2.
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 2 2 2` MEANS
    LIST `ea3 test sch 3 week` 2 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 2 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 2 0

-- Three weeks of 3 days each: item 7 gives 3, whose average is 3.
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 3 3 3` MEANS
    LIST `ea3 test sch 3 week` 3 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 3 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 3 0

-- Three weeks of 6 days each: item 7 gives 6, whose average is 6.
GIVETH A LIST OF `sch 3 Days required in a week`
`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 6 6 6` MEANS
    LIST `ea3 test sch 3 week` 6 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 6 0
       , `ea3 test sch 3 week` 6 0

GIVEN pattern IS A `sch 3 Arrangement of pay`
      monthly IS A `Pay for a period`
      weeks IS A `sch 3 item 5 Weeks for the average`
      approved IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 3 Facts about the pay`
`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` MEANS
    `sch 3 Facts about the pay` WITH
        `the arrangement of pay` IS pattern
        `the pay earned in the 14 days before the event` IS `ea3 test pay` 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
        `the days the employee actually worked in those 14 days` IS 0
        `the monthly pay` IS monthly
        `the days required in the first week` IS `ea3 test sch 3 week` 5 0
        `the days required in the second week` IS `ea3 test sch 3 week` 3 0
        `the weeks for the average` IS weeks
        `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved` IS approved

GIVEN earned IS A `Pay for a period`
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 3 Facts about the pay`
`ea3 test sch 3 piece facts` MEANS
    `sch 3 Facts about the pay` WITH
        `the arrangement of pay` IS `sch 3 item 1 piece rates`
        `the pay earned in the 14 days before the event` IS earned
        `the days the employee actually worked in those 14 days` IS days
        `the monthly pay` IS `ea3 test pay` 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
        `the days required in the first week` IS `ea3 test sch 3 week` 0 0
        `the days required in the second week` IS `ea3 test sch 3 week` 0 0
        `the weeks for the average` IS `ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)
        `the daily rate under a formula the Commissioner has approved` IS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- First Schedule (lines 5517-5525)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Items (1) to (7) name an occupation, and a person in one is specified whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 item (1) cleaners` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 item (2) construction workers` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 item (3) labourers` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 item (4) machine operators and assemblers` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 item (5) metal and machinery workers` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 item (6) train, bus, lorry and van drivers` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 item (7) train and bus inspectors` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Item (8): a workman, by another limb, employed on piece rates in the employer's premises.
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 an occupation that none of items (1) to (7) names` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Item (8) adds no one who is not already a workman by another limb, and not every piece-rate worker is in the employer's premises.
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 an occupation that none of items (1) to (7) names` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 an occupation that none of items (1) to (7) names` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 an occupation that none of items (1) to (7) names` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not known whether an item names the occupation: the Schedule does not say.
#ASSERT `sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 it is not known whether an item names the occupation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The seam: "workman" in s 2(1) takes the First Schedule's answer as limb (d).  A cleaner who meets none of the other limbs is a workman by limb (d) ...
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "workman" the person is one` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 item (1) cleaners` FALSE FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ... a person no item names is not a workman by limb (d) and so, meeting no other limb, is not a workman ...
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "workman" the person is one` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 an occupation that none of items (1) to (7) names` FALSE FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ... and where it is not known whether an item names the occupation, the Act's answer to "workman" is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "workman" the person is one` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`sch 1 the person is specified in the First Schedule` `sch 1 it is not known whether an item names the occupation` FALSE FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Second Schedule (lines 5534-5540)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT `sch 2 the registration fee` `Claimant who is an employee` EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `sch 2 the registration fee` `Claimant who is an employer` EQUALS JUST 20
-- A subcontractor for labour is in neither paragraph.
#ASSERT `sch 2 the registration fee` `Claimant who is a subcontractor for labour` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Third Schedule, item 7 and item 5 "week" (lines 5698-5711)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- 5 days of more than 5 hours: 5.  4 such days and 2 days of 5 hours or less (each half a day): 4 + 1 = 5.  Only half days: 3 / 2.
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` (`ea3 test sch 3 week` 5 0) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` (`ea3 test sch 3 week` 4 2) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 7 the number of working days in the week` (`ea3 test sch 3 week` 0 3) EQUALS 3 DIVIDED BY 2
-- "week" is 7 days commencing at midnight on a Sunday.
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 "week" the period is a week` (Date 4 1 2026) 7 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 "week" the period is a week` (Date 5 1 2026) 7 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 "week" the period is a week` (Date 4 1 2026) 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Third Schedule, item 5 (lines 5643-5696) and item 6 (lines 5701-5702)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- 3 weeks of 5, 5 and 2 days average 4; 3 weeks of 5, 3 and 6 average 14/3; a list of two weeks is not "the period of 3 weeks".
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`) EQUALS JUST (14 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average of the working days over the 3 weeks` (LIST `ea3 test sch 3 week` 5 0, `ea3 test sch 3 week` 5 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a), (b) and (c), limb (i): the 3 weeks immediately preceding; limb (ii): the alternative weeks, when the employee was in employment for less than 3 weeks.
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(a) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`)) EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(a) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` TRUE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`)) EQUALS JUST (14 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(b) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`)) EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(b) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` TRUE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`)) EQUALS JUST (14 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(c) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`)) EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(c) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` TRUE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`)) EQUALS JUST (14 DIVIDED BY 3)
-- The paragraph is picked by the purpose of the calculation; here the same weeks go in, so only a purpose-independent answer shows through.
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`)) EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` TRUE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`)) EQUALS JUST (14 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 3 6`)) EQUALS JUST 4
-- Item 6: in the third column paragraphs (a) and (b) are not applicable, so paragraph (c) applies whatever the purpose: its weeks are read, 3 (limb (i)) or 6 (limb (ii)), and never those of (a) or (b).
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 6 the average number of working days in a week for the third column` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 6 the average number of working days in a week for the third column` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 6 the average number of working days in a week for the third column` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 6 the average number of working days in a week for the third column` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 6 the average number of working days in a week for the third column` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 6 the average number of working days in a week for the third column` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` TRUE) EQUALS JUST 6
-- Item 5 itself reads the weeks of the paragraph the purpose names: (a) 4 or 14/3, (b) 1 or 2, (c) 3 or 6.
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(a) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST (14 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(a) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(a) the salary payable in lieu of notice of termination under section 11(1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST (14 DIVIDED BY 3)
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(b) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(b) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(b) the salary that may be deducted for absence from work under section 28(2)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(c) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5 the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` TRUE) EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 5(c) the average number of working days in a week` (`ea3 test sch 3 six weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` TRUE) EQUALS JUST 6

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Third Schedule, item 1 (lines 5554-5574): piece rates
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Earned in the 14 days: work 1,400; overtime 100; bonus 50; productivity incentive 30; reimbursement 5; travelling 15; food 20; housing 10; other allowance 40.
-- "Salary" leaves out the reimbursement and the travelling allowance: 1,400 + 100 + 50 + 30 + 20 + 10 + 40 = 1,650.
-- Second column takes out overtime, bonus, productivity, food and housing: 1,650 - 100 - 50 - 30 - 20 - 10 = 1,440.
-- Third column also takes out "any allowance however described" (the 40): 1,400.
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 1 the total salary for the gross rate of pay` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40) EQUALS 1440
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 1 the total salary for the basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40) EQUALS 1400
-- Over 10 days actually worked: 144 a day gross, 140 a day basic.
#ASSERT `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 piece facts` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40) 10) EQUALS JUST 144
#ASSERT `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 piece facts` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40) 10) EQUALS JUST 140
-- No day worked: the division has no quotient and the Schedule says nothing.
#ASSERT `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 piece facts` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40) 0) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 piece facts` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40) 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The two numerators agree with the s 2(1) terms for the same pay (the Schedule's words and the definitions' words say the same thing).
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 1 the total salary for the gross rate of pay` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40) EQUALS `s 2(1) "gross rate of pay" the amount` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40)
#ASSERT `sch 3 item 1 the total salary for the basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40) EQUALS `s 2(1) "basic rate of pay" the amount` (`ea3 test pay` 1400 100 50 30 5 15 20 10 40)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Third Schedule, items 2, 3 and 4 (lines 5573-5641): a monthly rate
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Monthly pay 2,600 for the work and a 52 allowance: gross 2,652, basic 2,600.
-- Item 2, 5 days required every week: gross 12 x 2,652 / (52 x 5) = 31,824 / 260 = 122.4; basic 12 x 2,600 / (52 x 5) = 120.
#ASSERT `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 item 2 monthly rate, the same number of days in every week` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 122.4
#ASSERT `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 item 2 monthly rate, the same number of days in every week` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 120
-- Item 3, 5 days one week and 3 the next: the average over 2 consecutive weeks is 4; gross 31,824 / 208 = 153; basic 31,200 / 208 = 150.
#ASSERT `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 item 3 monthly rate, a certain number of days in one week and a different number in the following week, in every period of 2 consecutive weeks` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 153
#ASSERT `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 item 3 monthly rate, a certain number of days in one week and a different number in the following week, in every period of 2 consecutive weeks` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 150
-- Item 4, 3 weeks of 5, 5 and 2 days: the average is 4, so the same 153 and 150.
#ASSERT `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 item 4 monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 153
#ASSERT `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 item 4 monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 150
-- Item 4 with a formula the Commissioner has approved: that formula's answer is the rate.
#ASSERT `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 item 4 monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) (JUST 140)) EQUALS JUST 140
#ASSERT `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 item 4 monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) (JUST 140)) EQUALS JUST 140
-- Item 4 where the weeks are not 3: item 5 has no average and the Schedule says nothing.
#ASSERT `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 item 4 monthly rate, different numbers of days in different weeks` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (LIST `ea3 test sch 3 week` 5 0) (LIST `ea3 test sch 3 week` 5 0)) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Item 2 where no day is required in a week: no quotient.
#ASSERT `sch 3 items 2 to 4 the formula` 2600 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 items 2 to 4 the formula` 2600 5 EQUALS JUST 120
-- An arrangement the Third Schedule does not list (an hourly, daily or weekly rate): the Schedule says nothing.
#ASSERT `sch 3 the gross rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 an arrangement the Third Schedule does not list` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 3 the basic rate of pay for one day` (`ea3 test sch 3 monthly facts` `sch 3 an arrangement the Third Schedule does not list` (`ea3 test pay` 2600 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 52) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks` `sch 3 item 5(c) any other case` FALSE (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`) (`ea3 test sch 3 weeks 5 5 2`)) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fourth Schedule (lines 5715-5753)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN type IS A `sch 4 Type of employee`
GIVETH A `sch 4 Facts about the pay`
`ea3 test sch 4 facts` MEANS
    `sch 4 Facts about the pay` WITH
        `the type of employee` IS type
        `the monthly basic rate of pay` IS 2288
        `the total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received` IS 528
        `the total number of hours worked in the week` IS 44
        `the actual hourly basic rate of pay` IS 15
        `the daily basic rate of pay` IS 96
        `the number of working hours per day` IS 8

GIVEN type IS A `sch 4 Type of employee`
      hours IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 4 Facts about the pay`
`ea3 test sch 4 facts with hours` MEANS
    `sch 4 Facts about the pay` WITH
        `the type of employee` IS type
        `the monthly basic rate of pay` IS 2288
        `the total weekly pay at the basic rate of pay received` IS 528
        `the total number of hours worked in the week` IS hours
        `the actual hourly basic rate of pay` IS 15
        `the daily basic rate of pay` IS 96
        `the number of working hours per day` IS hours

-- Items 1 and 2: 12 x 2,288 / (52 x 44) = 27,456 / 2,288 = 12, a workman or not.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts` `sch 4 item 1 a workman employed on a monthly rate of pay`) EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts` `sch 4 item 2 a non-workman employed on a monthly basic rate of pay`) EQUALS JUST 12
-- Items 4 and 5: the total weekly pay at the basic rate received, 528, divided by the 44 hours worked in the week.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts` `sch 4 item 4 a workman employed on piece rates`) EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts` `sch 4 item 5 a non-workman employed on piece rates`) EQUALS JUST 12
-- Items 6 and 7: the actual hourly basic rate of pay.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts` `sch 4 item 6 a workman employed on an hourly rate of pay`) EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts` `sch 4 item 7 a non-workman employed on an hourly rate of pay`) EQUALS JUST 15
-- Items 8 and 9: the daily basic rate of pay, 96, divided by the 8 working hours per day.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts` `sch 4 item 8 a workman employed on a daily rate of pay`) EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts` `sch 4 item 9 a non-workman employed on a daily rate of pay`) EQUALS JUST 12
-- No hours: no quotient.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts with hours` `sch 4 item 4 a workman employed on piece rates` 0) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts with hours` `sch 4 item 5 a non-workman employed on piece rates` 0) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts with hours` `sch 4 item 8 a workman employed on a daily rate of pay` 0) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts with hours` `sch 4 item 9 a non-workman employed on a daily rate of pay` 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A type the First column does not list (for example a weekly rate): the Schedule says nothing.
#ASSERT `sch 4 the hourly basic rate of pay` (`ea3 test sch 4 facts` `sch 4 a type of employee that the First column does not list`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fifth Schedule (lines 5778-5821)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN pattern IS A `sch 5 Work pattern`
      same IS A `sch 5 Work days in a week`
      fixed IS A LIST OF `sch 5 Work days in a week`
      preceding IS A LIST OF `sch 5 Work days in a week`
GIVETH A `sch 5 Facts about the work pattern`
`ea3 test sch 5 facts` MEANS
    `sch 5 Facts about the work pattern` WITH
        `the work pattern` IS pattern
        `the work days in a week when the number is the same in every week` IS same
        `the work days in each of the fixed weeks of the repeated pattern` IS fixed
        `the work days in each of the 3 weeks immediately preceding the day of confinement or the first day of leave` IS preceding

GIVEN full IS A NUMBER
      short IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `sch 5 Work days in a week`
`ea3 test sch 5 week` MEANS
    `sch 5 Work days in a week` WITH
        `work days of more than 5 hours` IS full
        `work days of 5 hours or shorter` IS short

-- Item 7: a day of 5 hours or shorter is half a day.
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 7 the number of work days in the week` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 7 the number of work days in the week` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 4 2) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 7 the number of work days in the week` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 0 3) EQUALS 3 DIVIDED BY 2
-- Item 5: a number that is not whole is rounded down to the nearest half day or whole day.
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 5 the number rounded down to the nearest half day or whole day` 17 EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 5 the number rounded down to the nearest half day or whole day` 17.4 EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 5 the number rounded down to the nearest half day or whole day` 17.5 EQUALS 17.5
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 5 the number rounded down to the nearest half day or whole day` 17.9 EQUALS 17.5
-- Item 4: the work pattern is the one immediately preceding the day of confinement or the first day of leave, whichever is the earlier.
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 4 the day by reference to which the work pattern is determined` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 4 the day by reference to which the work pattern is determined` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 4 the day by reference to which the work pattern is determined` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
-- Item 6: "week" and "work pattern".
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 6 "week" the period is a week` (Date 4 1 2026) 7 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 6 "week" the period is a week` (Date 6 1 2026) 7 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 6 "work pattern" the pattern is one` `sch 5 item 1 the number of work days is the same in every week` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 6 "work pattern" the pattern is one` `sch 5 item 2 the number of work days varies and there is a consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 6 "work pattern" the pattern is one` `sch 5 item 3 the number of work days varies and there is no consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 item 6 "work pattern" the pattern is one` `sch 5 a pattern that none of items 1, 2 and 3 describes` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Item 1: 4 x 5 work days in a week = 20; with 4 full days and 2 short days (5 work days) also 20.
#ASSERT `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` (`ea3 test sch 5 facts` `sch 5 item 1 the number of work days is the same in every week` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0) (LIST) (LIST)) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` (`ea3 test sch 5 facts` `sch 5 item 1 the number of work days is the same in every week` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 4 2) (LIST) (LIST)) EQUALS JUST 20
-- Item 2: weeks of 5 and 4 work days repeat; 4 x 9 / 2 = 18.
#ASSERT `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` (`ea3 test sch 5 facts` `sch 5 item 2 the number of work days varies and there is a consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 0 0) (LIST `ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0, `ea3 test sch 5 week` 4 0) (LIST)) EQUALS JUST 18
-- Item 2 with 5, 4 and 4 work days in 3 fixed weeks: 4 x 13 / 3 = 17.33..., rounded down to 17 (item 5).
#ASSERT `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` (`ea3 test sch 5 facts` `sch 5 item 2 the number of work days varies and there is a consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 0 0) (LIST `ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0, `ea3 test sch 5 week` 4 0, `ea3 test sch 5 week` 4 0) (LIST)) EQUALS JUST 17
-- Item 2 with no fixed week stated: no quotient.
#ASSERT `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` (`ea3 test sch 5 facts` `sch 5 item 2 the number of work days varies and there is a consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 0 0) (LIST) (LIST)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Item 3: the 3 weeks 5, 5 and 2 work days average 4; 4 x 4 = 16.
#ASSERT `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` (`ea3 test sch 5 facts` `sch 5 item 3 the number of work days varies and there is no consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 0 0) (LIST) (LIST `ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0, `ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0, `ea3 test sch 5 week` 2 0)) EQUALS JUST 16
-- Item 3 with 5, 5 and 3 work days: 4 x 13 / 3 = 17.33..., rounded down to 17.
#ASSERT `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` (`ea3 test sch 5 facts` `sch 5 item 3 the number of work days varies and there is no consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 0 0) (LIST) (LIST `ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0, `ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0, `ea3 test sch 5 week` 3 0)) EQUALS JUST 17
-- Item 3 with 2 weeks instead of 3: not "the period of 3 weeks".
#ASSERT `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` (`ea3 test sch 5 facts` `sch 5 item 3 the number of work days varies and there is no consistent or regular pattern repeated over a number of fixed weeks` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 0 0) (LIST) (LIST `ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0, `ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A pattern none of items 1, 2 and 3 describes: the Schedule says nothing.
#ASSERT `sch 5 the number of days on which the female employee is entitled to absent herself` (`ea3 test sch 5 facts` `sch 5 a pattern that none of items 1, 2 and 3 describes` (`ea3 test sch 5 week` 5 0) (LIST) (LIST)) EQUALS NOTHING
